# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RULE #1: nothing from the game (or any other proprietary source) is ever
# committed.
# Everything is built from files the user supplies at runtime.
# This file is the first line of defence; `cargo xtask policy` (also run by
# the pre-commit hook in .githooks/) is the second and is authoritative.
# See docs/asset-policy.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output
/target/
/tests/fixtures/*/target/

# Local configuration (contains paths to YOUR files)
/victory.toml

# Places people tend to drop data into. Keep data outside the repo instead.
/game/
/games/
/assets/
/data/
/dump/
/dumps/
/extracted/
/cache/
/out/

# Executables, libraries, symbols
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.lib
*.sys
*.obj
*.exp
*.ilk

# Console packages and containers
*.xvd
*.xvc
*.msixvc
*.xsp
*.cab
*.msi

# Typical game data (non-exhaustive on purpose; the policy check is an allowlist)
*.bin
# The one exception (docs/asset-policy.md): the BCPack format's constant tables.
!/crates/victory-formats/src/bcpack-tables.bin
*.dat
*.pak
*.rpf
*.dds
*.ktx
*.ktx2
*.dxbc
*.dxil
*.cso
*.spv
*.wav
*.xma
*.ogg
*.opus
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.bik
*.bk2
*.awc
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar

# The optional DLSS Frame Generation add-on for Ampere/Turing (dlssg_for_sm86,
# https://github.com/sdli1995/dlssg_for_sm86): NVIDIA's runtime, its kernel
# images and the proxy are third-party binaries, taken from that project's
# release and never committed (docs/dlss.md). The proxy itself is a *.dll,
# already ignored. Its logs and captures land here too.
/dlssg_sm86/
/dlssg_sm86.ini
/alternatives/
/dlssg_sm86.log

# Streamline's own logs (VICTORY_STREAMLINE_LOG)
/sl-logs/

# Editor / OS noise
.vs/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# NVIDIA's own files (Get-NVIDIA-DLSS.cmd fetches them from NVIDIA; never part of this repository)
/nvidia-sdk/
# What the F1 menu saved
/victory-settings.txt
/victory-settings.*.txt
